A few likely reasons this fails even with a seemingly correct XPath:

1. **Timing** — the popup may render slightly after page load; `page.click()` might fire before it's present.
2. **The XPath is too rigid/literal** — if you copied the exact structure `<app><div><div><div><div><button>`, Angular often injects extra wrapper divs dynamically, so an exact-depth XPath can break easily.

**Better approach — target the button by a stable attribute (id/class/text) instead of full DOM path:**
```python
("xpath", "//button[text()='OK']")
```
or
```python
("xpath", "//button[@class='some-stable-class']")
```

